{
 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Autix: train, evaluate and export both models\n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook retrains the **Xception** and **VGG19** autism-image classifiers with the fixes from the 2026 review, evaluates both on the same 300-image test set, and exports them for the browser demo in `web/`.\n",
    "\n",
    "**How to run it (Google Colab):**\n",
    "1. `Runtime \u2192 Change runtime type \u2192 T4 GPU`.\n",
    "2. `Runtime \u2192 Run all`. Allow Google Drive access when asked.\n",
    "3. At the end, `autix_export.zip` downloads. It is also saved in Google Drive under `MyDrive/autix_outputs/`.\n",
    "\n",
    "What changed from the 2022 notebooks:\n",
    "- Data is downloaded from Kaggle and labelled from file names, so nothing depends on a hand-organised Drive folder.\n",
    "- Each backbone gets its own ImageNet preprocessing (inside the model), instead of dividing by 255.\n",
    "- The head is `GlobalAveragePooling \u2192 Dropout \u2192 Dense(1)`. That is far smaller than `Flatten`, overfits less, and makes Class Activation Maps exact.\n",
    "- Training uses augmentation, early stopping with the best weights restored, then fine-tunes the top blocks.\n",
    "- Metrics are computed with `(y_true, y_pred)` in the right order, and ROC/AUC uses probabilities.\n",
    "- Seeds are fixed, and both models are scored on the same test set.\n",
    "\n",
    "This is an educational transfer-learning project, not a diagnostic tool."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Setup"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Training uses Colab's own TensorFlow. The browser converter (tensorflowjs) only works with\n",
    "# TensorFlow 2.19, so it gets its own small Python 3.12 environment, used in the export step.\n",
    "!pip install -q uv kagglehub\n",
    "!uv venv -q --allow-existing -p 3.12 /content/tfjs-env\n",
    "!uv pip install -q --python /content/tfjs-env/bin/python tensorflow==2.19.0 tensorflowjs==4.22.0 ydf==0.13.0 \"setuptools<81\"\n",
    "!/content/tfjs-env/bin/tensorflowjs_converter --version"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Imports"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import os, json, glob, hashlib, random, shutil, subprocess, datetime\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import tensorflow as tf\n",
    "import keras\n",
    "from keras import layers, ops\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "from sklearn.metrics import (accuracy_score, precision_score, recall_score, f1_score,\n",
    "                             roc_auc_score, roc_curve, confusion_matrix)\n",
    "from sklearn.model_selection import train_test_split\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"TensorFlow\", tf.__version__, \"| Keras\", keras.__version__)\n",
    "print(\"GPU:\", tf.config.list_physical_devices(\"GPU\") or \"none (training will be slow)\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Settings"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "SEED = 42\n",
    "IMG_SIZE = 224\n",
    "BATCH = 32\n",
    "EPOCHS_HEAD = 20        # stage 1: train only the new head\n",
    "EPOCHS_FINETUNE = 15    # stage 2: also train the top blocks of the backbone\n",
    "WEIGHTS = \"imagenet\"\n",
    "MODELS = [\"xception\", \"vgg19\"]\n",
    "EXPECTED_COUNTS = {\"train\": 2540, \"valid\": 100, \"test\": 300}\n",
    "\n",
    "keras.utils.set_random_seed(SEED)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Save results to Google Drive when it is available, so they survive the session.\n",
    "try:\n",
    "    from google.colab import drive\n",
    "    drive.mount(\"/content/drive\")\n",
    "    OUT_DIR = \"/content/drive/MyDrive/autix_outputs\"\n",
    "except Exception:\n",
    "    OUT_DIR = os.path.abspath(\"autix_outputs\")\n",
    "FIG_DIR = os.path.join(OUT_DIR, \"figures\")\n",
    "WEB_DIR = os.path.join(OUT_DIR, \"web_models\")\n",
    "for d in (OUT_DIR, FIG_DIR, WEB_DIR):\n",
    "    os.makedirs(d, exist_ok=True)\n",
    "print(\"Saving outputs to\", OUT_DIR)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Data\n",
    "The notebook first looks for `AutismDataset.zip` in your Google Drive (My Drive). If it isn't there, it downloads the Kaggle dataset [`cihan063/autism-image-data`](https://www.kaggle.com/datasets/cihan063/autism-image-data), which needs a Kaggle login."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "DRIVE_ZIP = \"/content/drive/MyDrive/AutismDataset.zip\"\n",
    "\n",
    "def find_dataset(base):\n",
    "    hits = [p for p in glob.glob(os.path.join(base, \"**\", \"AutismDataset\"), recursive=True)\n",
    "            if os.path.isdir(os.path.join(p, \"train\"))]\n",
    "    if not hits:\n",
    "        raise FileNotFoundError(f\"No AutismDataset folder with train/ inside {base}\")\n",
    "    return hits[0]\n",
    "\n",
    "if os.path.exists(DRIVE_ZIP):\n",
    "    shutil.unpack_archive(DRIVE_ZIP, \"/content/data\")\n",
    "    DATA_ROOT = find_dataset(\"/content/data\")\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    import kagglehub\n",
    "    try:\n",
    "        dl_path = kagglehub.dataset_download(\"cihan063/autism-image-data\")\n",
    "    except Exception as err:\n",
    "        raise RuntimeError(\n",
    "            \"Kaggle refused the download. Either upload AutismDataset.zip to My Drive and run this cell again, \"\n",
    "            \"or run `import kagglehub; kagglehub.login()` in a new cell first.\"\n",
    "        ) from err\n",
    "    DATA_ROOT = find_dataset(dl_path)\n",
    "print(\"Dataset at\", DATA_ROOT)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def label_for(path):\n",
    "    # valid/ uses class folders; train/ and test/ use names like Autistic.12.jpg\n",
    "    parent = os.path.basename(os.path.dirname(path))\n",
    "    name = parent if parent in (\"Autistic\", \"Non_Autistic\") else os.path.basename(path).split(\".\")[0]\n",
    "    if name == \"Autistic\":\n",
    "        return 1\n",
    "    if name == \"Non_Autistic\":\n",
    "        return 0\n",
    "    raise ValueError(f\"Cannot tell the label of {path}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "def list_split(split):\n",
    "    paths = sorted(p for p in glob.glob(os.path.join(DATA_ROOT, split, \"**\", \"*\"), recursive=True)\n",
    "                   if p.lower().endswith((\".jpg\", \".jpeg\", \".png\")))\n",
    "    return paths, [label_for(p) for p in paths]\n",
    "\n",
    "files = {s: list_split(s) for s in (\"train\", \"valid\", \"test\")}\n",
    "for s, (p, y) in files.items():\n",
    "    print(f\"{s:5s}: {len(p):4d} images, {sum(y):4d} autistic, {len(y) - sum(y):4d} non-autistic\")\n",
    "    if EXPECTED_COUNTS:\n",
    "        assert len(p) == EXPECTED_COUNTS[s], f\"expected {EXPECTED_COUNTS[s]} images in {s}\"\n",
    "\n",
    "# Leakage check: no identical image may appear in two splits.\n",
    "def md5(p):\n",
    "    with open(p, \"rb\") as f:\n",
    "        return hashlib.md5(f.read()).hexdigest()\n",
    "seen = {}\n",
    "for s, (paths, _) in files.items():\n",
    "    for p in paths:\n",
    "        seen.setdefault(md5(p), set()).add(s)\n",
    "cross = sum(1 for v in seen.values() if len(v) > 1)\n",
    "print(\"Images shared between splits:\", cross)\n",
    "assert cross == 0\n",
    "\n",
    "# The official validation split has only 100 images, which makes early stopping noisy.\n",
    "# Hold out 10% of train as well and validate on both. The test set is never touched.\n",
    "tr_p, extra_p, tr_y, extra_y = train_test_split(*files[\"train\"], test_size=0.10, stratify=files[\"train\"][1], random_state=SEED)\n",
    "train_p, train_y = tr_p, tr_y\n",
    "val_p, val_y = files[\"valid\"][0] + extra_p, files[\"valid\"][1] + extra_y\n",
    "test_p, test_y = files[\"test\"]\n",
    "print(f\"train {len(train_p)} | val {len(val_p)} | test {len(test_p)}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "AUTOTUNE = tf.data.AUTOTUNE\n",
    "\n",
    "def load_image(path, label):\n",
    "    img = tf.io.decode_image(tf.io.read_file(path), channels=3, expand_animations=False)\n",
    "    img = tf.image.resize(img, (IMG_SIZE, IMG_SIZE))   # float32, pixel values 0..255\n",
    "    return img, tf.cast(label, tf.float32)\n",
    "\n",
    "augment = keras.Sequential([\n",
    "    layers.RandomFlip(\"horizontal\"),\n",
    "    layers.RandomRotation(0.05),\n",
    "    layers.RandomZoom(0.1),\n",
    "    layers.RandomContrast(0.1),\n",
    "], name=\"augment\")\n",
    "\n",
    "def make_ds(paths, labels, training):\n",
    "    ds = tf.data.Dataset.from_tensor_slices((paths, labels))\n",
    "    if training:\n",
    "        ds = ds.shuffle(len(paths), seed=SEED)\n",
    "    ds = ds.map(load_image, num_parallel_calls=AUTOTUNE).cache()\n",
    "    ds = ds.batch(BATCH)\n",
    "    if training:\n",
    "        ds = ds.map(lambda x, y: (augment(x, training=True), y), num_parallel_calls=AUTOTUNE)\n",
    "    return ds.prefetch(AUTOTUNE)\n",
    "\n",
    "train_ds = make_ds(train_p, train_y, True)\n",
    "val_ds = make_ds(val_p, val_y, False)\n",
    "test_ds = make_ds(test_p, test_y, False)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Models\n",
    "Both models take raw RGB pixels (0..255) and do their own preprocessing, so the browser only has to resize the photo. The export version has two outputs: the probability and a 7x7 Class Activation Map."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "@keras.saving.register_keras_serializable(package=\"autix\")\n",
    "class CaffePreprocess(layers.Layer):\n",
    "    # VGG19's ImageNet preprocessing: RGB -> BGR, then subtract the ImageNet channel means.\n",
    "    def call(self, x):\n",
    "        return ops.flip(x, axis=-1) - ops.convert_to_tensor([103.939, 116.779, 123.68], dtype=x.dtype)\n",
    "\n",
    "@keras.saving.register_keras_serializable(package=\"autix\")\n",
    "class ClassActivationMap(layers.Layer):\n",
    "    # CAM for a GlobalAveragePooling -> Dense(1) head: the classifier's weights applied at every position.\n",
    "    def __init__(self, classifier, **kwargs):\n",
    "        super().__init__(**kwargs)\n",
    "        self.classifier = classifier\n",
    "    def call(self, features):\n",
    "        return ops.einsum(\"bhwc,co->bhw\", features, self.classifier.kernel)\n",
    "\n",
    "FINETUNE_PREFIXES = {\"xception\": (\"block13\", \"block14\"), \"vgg19\": (\"block5\",)}\n",
    "\n",
    "def build_model(name):\n",
    "    inp = keras.Input((IMG_SIZE, IMG_SIZE, 3), name=\"image\")\n",
    "    if name == \"xception\":\n",
    "        base = keras.applications.Xception(include_top=False, weights=WEIGHTS, input_shape=(IMG_SIZE, IMG_SIZE, 3))\n",
    "        x = layers.Rescaling(1 / 127.5, offset=-1, name=\"preprocess\")(inp)\n",
    "    else:\n",
    "        base = keras.applications.VGG19(include_top=False, weights=WEIGHTS, input_shape=(IMG_SIZE, IMG_SIZE, 3))\n",
    "        x = CaffePreprocess(name=\"preprocess\")(inp)\n",
    "    base.trainable = False\n",
    "    features = base(x, training=False)\n",
    "    pooled = layers.GlobalAveragePooling2D(name=\"gap\")(features)\n",
    "    pooled = layers.Dropout(0.3, name=\"dropout\")(pooled)\n",
    "    classifier = layers.Dense(1, activation=\"sigmoid\", name=\"classifier\")\n",
    "    prob = classifier(pooled)\n",
    "    model = keras.Model(inp, prob, name=name)\n",
    "    cam = ClassActivationMap(classifier, name=\"cam\")(features)\n",
    "    export_model = keras.Model(inp, {\"prob\": prob, \"cam\": cam}, name=f\"{name}_export\")\n",
    "    return model, export_model, base"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def compile_model(model, lr):\n",
    "    model.compile(optimizer=keras.optimizers.Adam(lr), loss=\"binary_crossentropy\",\n",
    "                  metrics=[\"accuracy\", keras.metrics.AUC(name=\"auc\")])\n",
    "\n",
    "def train(name, model, base):\n",
    "    stop = lambda patience: keras.callbacks.EarlyStopping(monitor=\"val_loss\", patience=patience, restore_best_weights=True)\n",
    "    print(f\"\\n=== {name}: stage 1, head only ===\")\n",
    "    compile_model(model, 1e-3)\n",
    "    h1 = model.fit(train_ds, validation_data=val_ds, epochs=EPOCHS_HEAD, callbacks=[stop(5)], verbose=2)\n",
    "\n",
    "    print(f\"\\n=== {name}: stage 2, fine-tune top blocks ===\")\n",
    "    base.trainable = True\n",
    "    for layer in base.layers:\n",
    "        layer.trainable = layer.name.startswith(FINETUNE_PREFIXES[name]) and not isinstance(layer, layers.BatchNormalization)\n",
    "    compile_model(model, 1e-5)\n",
    "    h2 = model.fit(train_ds, validation_data=val_ds, epochs=EPOCHS_FINETUNE, callbacks=[stop(4)], verbose=2)\n",
    "    return {k: h1.history[k] + h2.history[k] for k in h1.history}, len(h1.history[\"loss\"])"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def evaluate(name, model, history, stage1_epochs):\n",
    "    y_true = np.array(test_y)\n",
    "    y_prob = model.predict(test_ds, verbose=0).ravel()\n",
    "    y_pred = (y_prob >= 0.5).astype(int)\n",
    "    cm = confusion_matrix(y_true, y_pred)          # rows = actual, columns = predicted\n",
    "    m = {\n",
    "        \"accuracy\": float(accuracy_score(y_true, y_pred)),\n",
    "        \"precision\": float(precision_score(y_true, y_pred)),\n",
    "        \"recall\": float(recall_score(y_true, y_pred)),\n",
    "        \"f1\": float(f1_score(y_true, y_pred)),\n",
    "        \"auc\": float(roc_auc_score(y_true, y_prob)),\n",
    "        \"confusion_matrix\": cm.tolist(),\n",
    "        \"test_images\": int(len(y_true)),\n",
    "        \"epochs_trained\": len(history[\"loss\"]),\n",
    "    }\n",
    "    print(f\"{name}: \" + \", \".join(f\"{k} {v:.3f}\" for k, v in m.items() if isinstance(v, float)))\n",
    "\n",
    "    fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(4.2, 3.8))\n",
    "    ax.imshow(cm, cmap=\"Blues\")\n",
    "    for i in range(2):\n",
    "        for j in range(2):\n",
    "            ax.text(j, i, cm[i, j], ha=\"center\", va=\"center\", fontsize=14,\n",
    "                    color=\"white\" if cm[i, j] > cm.max() / 2 else \"black\")\n",
    "    ax.set_xticks([0, 1], [\"Non-autistic\", \"Autistic\"]); ax.set_yticks([0, 1], [\"Non-autistic\", \"Autistic\"])\n",
    "    ax.set_xlabel(\"Predicted\"); ax.set_ylabel(\"Actual\"); ax.set_title(f\"{name} confusion matrix (test)\")\n",
    "    fig.tight_layout(); fig.savefig(os.path.join(FIG_DIR, f\"{name}_confusion.png\"), dpi=150); plt.show()\n",
    "\n",
    "    fig, axes = plt.subplots(1, 2, figsize=(10, 3.5))\n",
    "    for ax, key in zip(axes, [\"loss\", \"accuracy\"]):\n",
    "        ax.plot(history[key], label=\"train\"); ax.plot(history[f\"val_{key}\"], label=\"validation\")\n",
    "        ax.axvline(stage1_epochs - 0.5, ls=\"--\", c=\"gray\", lw=1); ax.set_title(f\"{name} {key}\"); ax.set_xlabel(\"epoch\"); ax.legend()\n",
    "    fig.tight_layout(); fig.savefig(os.path.join(FIG_DIR, f\"{name}_training.png\"), dpi=150); plt.show()\n",
    "    return m, y_prob"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "TFJS_CONVERTER = \"/content/tfjs-env/bin/tensorflowjs_converter\"\n",
    "if not os.path.exists(TFJS_CONVERTER):\n",
    "    TFJS_CONVERTER = shutil.which(\"tensorflowjs_converter\")\n",
    "\n",
    "def export_for_web(name, export_model):\n",
    "    saved = os.path.join(OUT_DIR, \"savedmodel\", name)\n",
    "    shutil.rmtree(saved, ignore_errors=True)\n",
    "    export_model.export(saved, format=\"tf_saved_model\", verbose=False)\n",
    "\n",
    "    # Check the SavedModel gives the same answers as Keras before converting it.\n",
    "    batch = next(iter(test_ds))[0][:4]\n",
    "    keras_out = export_model.predict(batch, verbose=0)\n",
    "    loaded = tf.saved_model.load(saved)\n",
    "    served = loaded.serve(batch)\n",
    "    assert np.allclose(np.asarray(served[\"prob\"]), keras_out[\"prob\"], atol=1e-4)\n",
    "\n",
    "    out = os.path.join(WEB_DIR, name)\n",
    "    shutil.rmtree(out, ignore_errors=True)\n",
    "    subprocess.run([TFJS_CONVERTER, \"--input_format=tf_saved_model\", \"--output_format=tfjs_graph_model\",\n",
    "                    \"--signature_name=serving_default\", \"--saved_model_tags=serve\", \"--quantize_float16=*\",\n",
    "                    saved, out], check=True)\n",
    "    size = sum(os.path.getsize(p) for p in glob.glob(os.path.join(out, \"*\"))) / 1e6\n",
    "    print(f\"{name}: browser model written to {out} ({size:.1f} MB)\")\n",
    "    return round(size, 1)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Train, evaluate and export\n",
    "On a T4 GPU this takes roughly 10 to 20 minutes per model."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "results, probs = {}, {}\n",
    "for name in MODELS:\n",
    "    keras.utils.set_random_seed(SEED)\n",
    "    model, export_model, base = build_model(name)\n",
    "    history, stage1 = train(name, model, base)\n",
    "    results[name], probs[name] = evaluate(name, model, history, stage1)\n",
    "    model.save(os.path.join(OUT_DIR, f\"{name}.keras\"))\n",
    "    results[name][\"browser_model_mb\"] = export_for_web(name, export_model)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(5, 4.5))\n",
    "for name in MODELS:\n",
    "    fpr, tpr, _ = roc_curve(test_y, probs[name])\n",
    "    ax.plot(fpr, tpr, label=f\"{name} (AUC {results[name]['auc']:.3f})\")\n",
    "ax.plot([0, 1], [0, 1], ls=\"--\", c=\"gray\", lw=1)\n",
    "ax.set_xlabel(\"False positive rate\"); ax.set_ylabel(\"True positive rate\"); ax.set_title(\"ROC on the test set\"); ax.legend()\n",
    "fig.tight_layout(); fig.savefig(os.path.join(FIG_DIR, \"roc.png\"), dpi=150); plt.show()\n",
    "\n",
    "summary = {\n",
    "    \"models\": results,\n",
    "    \"dataset\": \"kaggle.com/datasets/cihan063/autism-image-data\",\n",
    "    \"test_set\": \"official test split, 150 autistic + 150 non-autistic\",\n",
    "    \"threshold\": 0.5,\n",
    "    \"seed\": SEED,\n",
    "    \"tensorflow\": tf.__version__,\n",
    "    \"trained_on\": datetime.date.today().isoformat(),\n",
    "}\n",
    "with open(os.path.join(WEB_DIR, \"metrics.json\"), \"w\") as f:\n",
    "    json.dump(summary, f, indent=2)\n",
    "print(json.dumps({k: {m: round(v, 3) for m, v in r.items() if isinstance(v, float)} for k, r in results.items()}, indent=2))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Only the browser models and figures go in the zip.\n",
    "staging = \"/tmp/autix_export\"\n",
    "shutil.rmtree(staging, ignore_errors=True)\n",
    "shutil.copytree(WEB_DIR, os.path.join(staging, \"models\"))\n",
    "shutil.copytree(FIG_DIR, os.path.join(staging, \"figures\"))\n",
    "zip_path = shutil.make_archive(os.path.join(OUT_DIR, \"autix_export\"), \"zip\", staging)\n",
    "print(\"Export:\", zip_path)\n",
    "try:\n",
    "    from google.colab import files as colab_files\n",
    "    colab_files.download(zip_path)\n",
    "except Exception:\n",
    "    pass"
   ]
  },
  
